{
  "id": "heat-haze-mirage",
  "name": "Heat Haze Mirage",
  "url": "shaders/heat-haze-mirage.wgsl",
  "category": "image",
  "description": "Inferior mirage from a real refractive-index gradient: light curvature follows dn/dy through the hot layer and the lateral deflection accumulates as the square of the path, rather than scaling linearly with a noise sample. Past the critical gradient a vertically mirrored sample folds in, reproducing the false 'water' and doubled horizon of a road mirage. Fixes a depth clobber that overwrote scene geometry with the heat column, and replaces a hard 1.3 clamp with ACES.",
